# i18n — translate every word

## Rule
- **No hardcoded user-facing English** in storefront or customer UI (buttons, labels, placeholders, empty states, errors, toasts, aria-labels that users hear/see).
- Use `next-intl`: `useTranslations` / `getTranslations`.
- Add keys to **`messages/en.json` first**, then mirror into **all** locale files under `messages/` (`ar`, `de`, `es`, `fr`, `nl`, `pl`, `pt`, `ru`, `tr`, `ur`, …).
- Keep key structure namespaced (`common`, `header`, `cart`, `checkout`, `catalog`, `products`, `account`, …).

## Examples

```tsx
// BAD
<button>Add to Cart</button>

// GOOD
const t = useTranslations("common");
<button>{t("addToCart")}</button>
```

## Admin UI
- Prefer translation keys for admin chrome too when adding new screens; at minimum never leave storefront strings untranslated.
- Dynamic CMS/admin-managed content (product names, section titles from DB) is data — not message-file copy — but **UI chrome** around it must be translated.

## Checklist before finishing a UI task
- [ ] No new literal user-facing strings in TSX
- [ ] Keys added to `en.json`
- [ ] Same keys added to every other `messages/*.json`
